# CI workflow rules

- `.github/workflows/` files are gate files: the guard blocks edits unless a human approves them (`ai-gate-change-approved`). Explain every change to triggers, permissions, or required checks in the PR.
- CI runs the same gate as local work: `./scripts/verify.sh`. Do not maintain a second list of checks in YAML; add a check to the gate script instead.
- Never weaken a gate step: no `continue-on-error: true`, `|| true`, `if: false`, removed jobs, or narrowed `paths` filters to get green.
- Set `permissions:` explicitly, starting from `contents: read`, and grant more only to the job that needs it.
- Secrets go in `env:` on the step or job that uses them, never at workflow level. Never print them, and never run pull request code with secrets (`pull_request_target` plus a checkout of the PR head).
- Actions from `actions/*` and other reviewed publishers may use a major tag; any other publisher is pinned to a full commit SHA.
- Use `concurrency` so a new push cancels the superseded pull request run; keep runs on the default branch so every merged commit has a result.
- Release and deploy jobs run on manual dispatch or tags, only from a commit whose gate is green. Never deploy from an artifact built by an unverified run.
- macOS runners bill at 10x Linux minutes on private repositories. Run macOS jobs only where the check needs macOS (iOS builds), not on every push.
